 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "users is a list of [name, group] rows. Pair users so that the two users of a pair always come from different groups. Greedy rule: while at least two groups still have unpaired users, take the group with the most unpaired users and the group with the second most (ties to the smaller group name in code-point order), and pair the earliest-listed unpaired user of the first with the earliest-listed unpaired user of the second, recording [user of the larger group, user of the other group]. Return the pairs in the order formed; users left unpaired are not reported.",
  "provenance": [
